gohard is a VHDL language server with a built-in simulator.

Usage:
  gohard <command> [flags] [arguments]

Commands:
  check    parse and analyze VHDL; with --sim, run testbenches
  config   check gohard.yaml or print its JSON schema
  fmt      format VHDL files in place, or check formatting
  help     show help for gohard or one command
  libs     find vendor libraries and print gohard.yaml lines
  lsp      run the language server, or one language-server action
  parse    print the concrete syntax tree of a file
  trace    export a simulation trace to VCD or FST
  version  print the gohard version

Global flags:
  -h, --help         show help
  -p, --jobs N       run at most N parallel jobs (output never depends on N)
      --output FILE  write standard output to FILE (a temp file, then rename)

Exit codes:
  0    clean (warnings and hints do not fail a run)
  1    the design has problems (any warning with --strict)
  2    tool or setup failure, or an opaque unit; wins over 1
  130  interrupted (Ctrl-C)
  143  terminated (SIGTERM)

Run 'gohard help <command>' for the flags of one command.
